1
00:01:01,120 --> 00:01:06,280
Taming The Husband

2
00:01:06,400 --> 00:01:08,920
Episode 6

3
00:01:09,800 --> 00:01:11,120
Send out whoever's in charge.

4
00:01:11,280 --> 00:01:12,360
I'm here to buy back the jade.

5
00:01:12,440 --> 00:01:14,600
Three hundred taels.
Not a wen more or less.

6
00:01:15,240 --> 00:01:17,680
Three hundred taels won't cover it.

7
00:01:20,080 --> 00:01:21,400
Half a month ago,

8
00:01:21,640 --> 00:01:22,960
your brother did bring in a jade carving

9
00:01:23,040 --> 00:01:24,720
to settle a debt of 300 taels.

10
00:01:25,120 --> 00:01:27,560
Then he went straight back to gambling.

11
00:01:27,960 --> 00:01:30,280
He lost, borrowed, and gambled again.

12
00:01:30,520 --> 00:01:31,520
Altogether,

13
00:01:31,920 --> 00:01:34,760
he borrowed 3,263 taels.

14
00:01:35,080 --> 00:01:36,400
At 30% interest a month,

15
00:01:36,560 --> 00:01:39,000
with interest up to today,

16
00:01:39,080 --> 00:01:40,480
you owe me

17
00:01:40,640 --> 00:01:42,880
3,720 taels.

18
00:01:44,280 --> 00:01:47,080
Thirty percent?
Even loan sharks aren't that ruthless!

19
00:01:47,400 --> 00:01:49,760
Listen.
Take the money and call it settled,

20
00:01:49,840 --> 00:01:51,480
or I'll go to the magistrate.

21
00:01:51,720 --> 00:01:54,200
The magistrate? You can't even read.

22
00:01:54,280 --> 00:01:55,960
How would you write a petition?

23
00:01:56,600 --> 00:01:58,720
Even if you paid someone to write it,

24
00:01:58,800 --> 00:01:59,960
going through the magistrate's office

25
00:02:00,040 --> 00:02:01,880
takes 10 days or two weeks, at best.

26
00:02:02,040 --> 00:02:03,960
Let me remind you, here,

27
00:02:04,040 --> 00:02:05,800
the interest adds up every day.

28
00:02:05,880 --> 00:02:07,000
Every extra day

29
00:02:07,080 --> 00:02:08,680
will cost you dozens of taels.

30
00:02:09,000 --> 00:02:10,800
And if you lose the case,

31
00:02:10,880 --> 00:02:13,880
that debt… You'd never pay it off.

32
00:02:15,520 --> 00:02:16,760
You know I can't read?

33
00:02:17,600 --> 00:02:18,760
You know who I am?

34
00:02:19,640 --> 00:02:20,640
Who told you?

35
00:02:20,840 --> 00:02:21,880
Two months ago,

36
00:02:22,200 --> 00:02:24,080
a scholar came to discuss marrying you.

37
00:02:24,600 --> 00:02:26,520
You tricked him into buying pork,

38
00:02:27,040 --> 00:02:29,600
then married into the wealthy Xie family.

39
00:02:29,840 --> 00:02:31,800
You made a fool of him.

40
00:02:32,160 --> 00:02:33,400
He's an honest man,

41
00:02:33,480 --> 00:02:35,200
so he won't make trouble for you.

42
00:02:35,560 --> 00:02:38,440
But I, his uncle,

43
00:02:38,520 --> 00:02:40,440
can't just let that pass.

44
00:02:41,080 --> 00:02:43,960
Today, if I get some satisfaction,

45
00:02:44,360 --> 00:02:46,280
perhaps I'll take pity on you

46
00:02:47,360 --> 00:02:48,960
and restore the jade to its owner.

47
00:02:49,040 --> 00:02:51,720
Restore what?
Whatever you've got, bring it on!

48
00:02:51,800 --> 00:02:53,480
If you lose, you give me back the jade.

49
00:02:54,600 --> 00:02:56,680
Lady Jin, this is a gambling house.

50
00:02:56,760 --> 00:02:57,960
Gambling made my fortune.

51
00:02:58,040 --> 00:03:00,160
Why would I fight you?

52
00:03:01,000 --> 00:03:02,080
Play one game with me.

53
00:03:02,320 --> 00:03:03,680
If you win,

54
00:03:03,840 --> 00:03:08,160
your brother's debts are wiped out.
Do you dare?

55
00:03:08,240 --> 00:03:09,720
-Play him! Play him!
-Play him!

56
00:03:09,800 --> 00:03:10,960
-Play him!
-Go on!

57
00:03:11,320 --> 00:03:14,800
Play him! Play him!

58
00:03:14,880 --> 00:03:17,560
No! Don't gamble! Don't!

59
00:03:17,640 --> 00:03:18,640
-Play! Play!
-Baoyu!

60
00:03:18,720 --> 00:03:19,760
We'll play! We'll play!

61
00:03:19,840 --> 00:03:22,040
Baozhu, play him!

62
00:03:22,560 --> 00:03:24,200
Win this, and I'm set for life!

63
00:03:24,280 --> 00:03:25,560
-Baozhu!
-Shut up!

64
00:03:25,920 --> 00:03:26,920
Nine out of ten gamblers lose!

65
00:03:27,120 --> 00:03:28,840
Keep barking,
and I'll rip your mouth apart!

66
00:03:28,920 --> 00:03:30,800
He owes the money. I set the terms.

67
00:03:30,880 --> 00:03:33,600
Refuse,
and the interest will keep compounding.

68
00:03:33,680 --> 00:03:35,080
You'd never clear the debt.

69
00:03:35,280 --> 00:03:37,360
Will you save him or watch him die?

70
00:03:37,560 --> 00:03:38,640
Your choice.

71
00:03:39,840 --> 00:03:43,240
I'm not gambling.
I only want to buy my jade back.

72
00:03:43,480 --> 00:03:45,840
As for him,
kill him, cut him up. I don't care.

73
00:03:46,040 --> 00:03:47,920
No! You can't kill him!

74
00:03:48,600 --> 00:03:49,960
You can't kill him!

75
00:03:50,440 --> 00:03:51,880
Baoyu started his lessons at six,

76
00:03:52,040 --> 00:03:53,440
learning to read and recite poetry.

77
00:03:53,680 --> 00:03:54,960
He worked so hard.

78
00:03:55,280 --> 00:03:58,000
Even when he was ill,
he wouldn't neglect his studies.

79
00:03:58,080 --> 00:04:00,760
His teachers said he had a bright future.

80
00:04:02,240 --> 00:04:03,320
Your father died young.

81
00:04:03,880 --> 00:04:06,480
I worked day and night to raise you.

82
00:04:06,840 --> 00:04:08,480
Now you've married into wealth,

83
00:04:08,600 --> 00:04:10,160
you won't acknowledge your own mother!

84
00:04:11,520 --> 00:04:14,320
You… You can hit me, curse me,

85
00:04:14,400 --> 00:04:16,240
but please, have mercy.

86
00:04:16,960 --> 00:04:18,080
Save him.

87
00:04:18,320 --> 00:04:20,240
Save him! Please save him!

88
00:04:20,320 --> 00:04:22,720
I'm begging you! Save him!

89
00:04:23,680 --> 00:04:24,880
Please!

90
00:04:25,560 --> 00:04:27,120
I'm begging you!

91
00:04:27,280 --> 00:04:28,800
Then let everyone see

92
00:04:30,200 --> 00:04:33,200
whose hands have known nothing but luxury,

93
00:04:33,480 --> 00:04:35,280
and whose have worked day and night!

94
00:04:39,920 --> 00:04:42,720
Madam Huang, out of respect for your age,

95
00:04:42,960 --> 00:04:44,280
I call you Madam Huang.

96
00:04:45,120 --> 00:04:46,880
You didn't give birth to me.

97
00:04:47,080 --> 00:04:48,400
You certainly didn't raise me!

98
00:04:48,800 --> 00:04:49,880
If anyone doubts me,

99
00:04:49,960 --> 00:04:51,400
go and ask in the village

100
00:04:52,000 --> 00:04:53,600
whether there's a Jin family

101
00:04:53,800 --> 00:04:55,360
living entirely off one person!

102
00:04:56,000 --> 00:04:59,080
Isn't it enough
that you bleed me dry every day?

103
00:04:59,880 --> 00:05:01,600
Even marriage hasn't given me any peace!

104
00:05:02,000 --> 00:05:03,320
And you have the nerve to blame me?

105
00:05:03,680 --> 00:05:05,880
Listen. My only mistake

106
00:05:06,120 --> 00:05:08,200
was keeping you all so fat and well fed,

107
00:05:08,280 --> 00:05:10,160
you've lost all sense of shame
and all human decency!

108
00:05:10,760 --> 00:05:12,480
Your precious son promised me

109
00:05:12,960 --> 00:05:15,520
that if he gambled again,
I'd chop off one of his hands.

110
00:05:15,880 --> 00:05:17,800
I merely broke his arm.

111
00:05:18,040 --> 00:05:19,480
He's lucky I haven't disowned him!

112
00:05:39,120 --> 00:05:40,200
Baoyu!

113
00:05:40,320 --> 00:05:41,320
Baoyu!

114
00:05:43,920 --> 00:05:46,920
Then… Then cut your ties.

115
00:05:47,680 --> 00:05:49,720
Jin Baozhu, if you win this game,

116
00:05:49,920 --> 00:05:51,880
the Jin family will have no claim on you.

117
00:05:52,520 --> 00:05:54,880
They'll never trouble you again.

118
00:05:56,400 --> 00:05:57,920
Do you accept?

119
00:06:00,680 --> 00:06:01,760
Baoyu!

120
00:06:06,600 --> 00:06:07,680
We're all human.

121
00:06:07,880 --> 00:06:10,960
Surely you have some compassion?

122
00:06:11,360 --> 00:06:13,960
Would you really watch your own brother

123
00:06:14,360 --> 00:06:16,000
die without lifting a finger?

124
00:06:16,440 --> 00:06:23,160
Play him! Play him!

125
00:06:23,240 --> 00:06:24,280
Baoyu!

126
00:06:24,800 --> 00:06:26,800
<i>Don't gamble! Don't!</i>

127
00:06:33,480 --> 00:06:34,560
I'll play him.

128
00:06:35,640 --> 00:06:38,000
Play him! Play him!

129
00:06:38,880 --> 00:06:41,360
Isn't that
the Xie family's second young master?

130
00:06:41,440 --> 00:06:42,480
That's him.

131
00:06:59,120 --> 00:07:00,720
What a wind we're having today.

132
00:07:01,040 --> 00:07:02,440
It's blown Yangzhou's great scholar,

133
00:07:02,520 --> 00:07:04,240
Young Master Xie, right to my door.

134
00:07:04,360 --> 00:07:05,880
It's been a while, Master Qian.

135
00:07:06,840 --> 00:07:08,520
You haven't changed a bit.

136
00:07:08,840 --> 00:07:11,480
As petty and small-minded as ever.

137
00:07:11,760 --> 00:07:13,520
I used to come here often,

138
00:07:13,600 --> 00:07:14,720
and I never lost.

139
00:07:15,120 --> 00:07:16,840
You tried to challenge me several times,

140
00:07:16,920 --> 00:07:18,240
but I always turned you down.

141
00:07:19,960 --> 00:07:21,400
No time like the present.

142
00:07:21,680 --> 00:07:23,120
Since we're both here,

143
00:07:23,280 --> 00:07:25,320
let's settle our scores, old and new.

144
00:07:25,520 --> 00:07:27,000
Play a game with me.

145
00:07:27,600 --> 00:07:28,840
What do you say?

146
00:07:33,040 --> 00:07:35,680
Today's game is Ghost Tower.

147
00:07:36,040 --> 00:07:37,320
The rules are simple.

148
00:07:37,880 --> 00:07:39,920
We take 54 rectangular wooden blocks,

149
00:07:40,160 --> 00:07:42,320
stack them in alternating layers of three,

150
00:07:42,440 --> 00:07:44,880
and build an 18-story tower.

151
00:07:45,080 --> 00:07:47,400
We take turns removing blocks from it.

152
00:07:47,480 --> 00:07:49,680
Whoever brings it down loses.

153
00:07:49,960 --> 00:07:52,280
If half an incense stick burns down
before you move, you lose.

154
00:07:52,360 --> 00:07:55,840
If you win,
you take both the jade and your brother.

155
00:07:56,000 --> 00:07:59,720
If I win, you pay double Jin Baoyu's debt.

156
00:08:00,240 --> 00:08:01,440
Any objections?

157
00:08:03,440 --> 00:08:05,160
-None.
-Good.

158
00:08:05,720 --> 00:08:07,600
Usually, in Ghost Tower,

159
00:08:07,680 --> 00:08:09,000
we pull out wooden blocks.

160
00:08:09,120 --> 00:08:10,440
Rather dull.

161
00:08:10,520 --> 00:08:12,800
Today, let's try something new.

162
00:08:18,760 --> 00:08:20,720
Treasure Bowl

163
00:08:22,120 --> 00:08:24,040
We'll use ice blocks

164
00:08:24,440 --> 00:08:26,600
instead of wood.

165
00:08:27,040 --> 00:08:28,800
We'll use a date spinner
to decide who goes first.

166
00:08:28,880 --> 00:08:30,320
Red goes first, black goes second.

167
00:08:45,040 --> 00:08:46,080
Please.

168
00:09:16,520 --> 00:09:17,600
He's pulled out another one!

169
00:09:17,800 --> 00:09:19,400
Why does he take one, but you take two?

170
00:09:19,480 --> 00:09:24,400
Lady Jin, I never said
you could take only one block per turn.

171
00:09:25,200 --> 00:09:26,760
In a gambling house,

172
00:09:26,840 --> 00:09:31,400
anything not expressly forbidden
is allowed. Am I right?

173
00:09:31,520 --> 00:09:32,520
He's right!

174
00:09:32,880 --> 00:09:34,120
That's how it works.

175
00:09:34,360 --> 00:09:35,400
Exactly.

176
00:09:35,760 --> 00:09:36,760
That makes sense.

177
00:09:38,600 --> 00:09:40,720
Xi, how was that?

178
00:09:41,680 --> 00:09:44,000
Your big brother
got revenge for you, didn't he?

179
00:09:44,440 --> 00:09:46,080
Your little brother was the clever one.

180
00:09:46,400 --> 00:09:48,440
He knew Qian Zhenshan was an old friend.

181
00:09:48,760 --> 00:09:50,200
Xie Heng is the only brother I have.

182
00:09:50,600 --> 00:09:52,120
Another word,
and I'll pull your tongue out!

183
00:10:10,280 --> 00:10:11,280
Brilliant! Brilliant!

184
00:10:11,400 --> 00:10:12,720
Amazing! So steady!

185
00:10:16,200 --> 00:10:17,240
Your turn.

186
00:10:35,200 --> 00:10:36,200
Good! Good!

187
00:10:36,360 --> 00:10:37,480
Brilliant! Brilliant!

188
00:10:51,520 --> 00:10:53,720
Wait. Salt melts ice.

189
00:10:54,000 --> 00:10:55,280
You just picked up some salt.

190
00:10:56,120 --> 00:10:57,800
When you remove an ice block,

191
00:10:58,440 --> 00:11:00,440
you could rub salt on the joints.

192
00:11:00,920 --> 00:11:02,000
By my turn,

193
00:11:02,360 --> 00:11:03,800
the tower would have melted and collapsed.

194
00:11:04,240 --> 00:11:05,600
How could I prove my innocence?

195
00:11:10,080 --> 00:11:11,160
Master Qian, isn't that cheating?

196
00:11:11,280 --> 00:11:12,640
You're playing dirty, Master Qian!

197
00:11:13,480 --> 00:11:15,160
It's only a few grains of salt.

198
00:11:16,760 --> 00:11:17,800
I'll wipe them off.

199
00:11:31,600 --> 00:11:32,680
Fine.

200
00:11:34,080 --> 00:11:35,920
Brilliant! Brilliant!
Amazing!

201
00:11:36,640 --> 00:11:37,720
Your turn.

202
00:11:38,920 --> 00:11:40,240
He's in trouble now.

203
00:11:54,520 --> 00:11:55,640
Make a fuss, if you like.

204
00:11:55,720 --> 00:11:58,680
If that tower falls,
your husband is finished.

205
00:12:00,200 --> 00:12:01,920
<i>Anything not expressly forbidden</i>
<i>is allowed.</i>

206
00:12:02,080 --> 00:12:04,000
<i>If I expose them now,</i>

207
00:12:04,240 --> 00:12:05,920
<i>they might not even be disqualified,</i>

208
00:12:06,160 --> 00:12:07,240
<i>and I could startle Xie Yan.</i>

209
00:12:17,120 --> 00:12:18,160
<i>This is bad.</i>

210
00:12:31,160 --> 00:12:32,920
Half the incense stick is almost gone.

211
00:12:33,280 --> 00:12:36,080
Young Master Xie,
if you don't make your move,

212
00:12:36,360 --> 00:12:39,040
the tower will melt by itself.

213
00:12:39,520 --> 00:12:40,560
Pull one out!

214
00:12:40,680 --> 00:12:42,160
Go on! Hurry up and pull one!

215
00:12:42,240 --> 00:12:43,440
Pull one, Young Master Xie!

216
00:12:43,720 --> 00:12:44,800
What are you waiting for?

217
00:12:45,560 --> 00:12:47,600
Hurry up!
What's taking so long?

218
00:12:56,640 --> 00:12:57,720
Brilliant!

219
00:12:58,920 --> 00:13:00,480
Good! Good!

220
00:13:00,600 --> 00:13:01,760
Amazing! Absolutely amazing!

221
00:13:01,840 --> 00:13:04,320
Master Qian, I'm out of moves.

222
00:13:05,320 --> 00:13:06,560
Please, go on.

223
00:13:46,360 --> 00:13:47,800
He's sure to win now!

224
00:13:47,880 --> 00:13:49,160
Master Qian's the best!

225
00:13:57,840 --> 00:13:59,040
It fell after all!

226
00:14:00,440 --> 00:14:02,600
So close!
Master Qian lost!

227
00:14:05,040 --> 00:14:06,080
We won!

228
00:14:08,160 --> 00:14:09,160
Xi.

229
00:14:10,400 --> 00:14:11,560
Well played.

230
00:14:14,680 --> 00:14:15,720
Wait!

231
00:14:16,840 --> 00:14:18,120
Young Master Xie,

232
00:14:18,560 --> 00:14:20,360
you were supposed

233
00:14:20,480 --> 00:14:22,280
to take three turns in all.

234
00:14:22,680 --> 00:14:24,080
But this tray

235
00:14:24,280 --> 00:14:25,720
has only two ice blocks.

236
00:14:25,800 --> 00:14:27,320
That means on your last turn,

237
00:14:27,800 --> 00:14:29,080
you didn't take one at all!

238
00:14:29,760 --> 00:14:31,480
I made the rules quite clear.

239
00:14:31,680 --> 00:14:33,200
We were to take turns

240
00:14:33,280 --> 00:14:34,480
removing blocks from the ice tower.

241
00:14:34,800 --> 00:14:36,560
You cheated.

242
00:14:37,000 --> 00:14:39,760
This game doesn't count!

243
00:14:41,880 --> 00:14:43,480
He's right! He's right!

244
00:14:43,760 --> 00:14:45,080
From start to finish,

245
00:14:45,680 --> 00:14:48,680
I only took two turns. Didn't I?

246
00:14:56,520 --> 00:14:58,760
It isn't that
I failed to take a block on my turn.

247
00:14:59,280 --> 00:15:01,320
Your turn was taking so long,

248
00:15:01,560 --> 00:15:02,960
I grew impatient

249
00:15:03,320 --> 00:15:06,480
and took a block
to play with while I waited.

250
00:15:07,640 --> 00:15:10,480
Is that not allowed?
You said it yourself,

251
00:15:10,920 --> 00:15:14,400
"Anything not expressly
forbidden is allowed."

252
00:15:14,640 --> 00:15:16,120
Yes, that's true.

253
00:15:16,640 --> 00:15:18,000
Master Qian said so himself.

254
00:15:18,880 --> 00:15:21,560
Besides, I told you quite plainly,

255
00:15:22,080 --> 00:15:24,160
"I'm out of moves. Please, go on."

256
00:15:24,920 --> 00:15:26,280
And you agreed, didn't you?

257
00:15:27,080 --> 00:15:28,160
Impossible!

258
00:15:29,000 --> 00:15:30,520
How could I lose to you?

259
00:15:31,000 --> 00:15:32,480
To a cripple,

260
00:15:32,960 --> 00:15:35,320
a sick wretch with one foot in the grave!

261
00:15:35,400 --> 00:15:36,480
-Shut your mouth!
-You--

262
00:15:37,200 --> 00:15:38,320
My husband, Xie Yan,

263
00:15:38,400 --> 00:15:40,200
is Yangzhou's renowned scholar!

264
00:15:40,360 --> 00:15:42,000
He came first in all three exams!

265
00:15:42,080 --> 00:15:43,400
Who are you to insult him?

266
00:15:57,320 --> 00:15:58,520
Baozhu, let's go.

267
00:16:01,840 --> 00:16:03,280
Where did you learn to be so smooth?

268
00:16:03,920 --> 00:16:05,520
-You know?
-Of course I know.

269
00:16:05,680 --> 00:16:06,720
How did you know?

270
00:16:07,040 --> 00:16:08,040
I'm clever, aren't I?

271
00:16:20,760 --> 00:16:22,880
Madam hasn't been feeling well.

272
00:16:23,360 --> 00:16:24,840
She's already gone to bed.

273
00:16:25,240 --> 00:16:27,040
I've brought some tonic herbs.

274
00:16:27,440 --> 00:16:28,720
Make sure you brew them for her.

275
00:16:29,000 --> 00:16:30,080
Yes, sir.

276
00:16:58,240 --> 00:17:00,800
Madam seems very fond of this kite.

277
00:17:00,880 --> 00:17:02,520
It's too worn to mend,

278
00:17:03,080 --> 00:17:04,960
but she insists on keeping it up.

279
00:17:06,160 --> 00:17:09,040
I hear Wanjun has found Yan a bride.

280
00:17:09,800 --> 00:17:11,240
What's the girl like?

281
00:17:11,600 --> 00:17:13,080
It's not my place to say, sir.

282
00:17:19,280 --> 00:17:21,040
If she's won Yan's favor,

283
00:17:21,560 --> 00:17:24,040
she must be very understanding,

284
00:17:24,520 --> 00:17:25,600
gentle and clever.

285
00:17:41,400 --> 00:17:43,280
Lady Qin! The master's back!

286
00:17:43,600 --> 00:17:45,800
Lady Qin! The master's back!

287
00:17:48,320 --> 00:17:49,720
Chengzong!

288
00:17:51,640 --> 00:17:53,200
You're finally home!

289
00:17:54,920 --> 00:17:56,880
I've been longing for your return.

290
00:17:59,120 --> 00:18:01,360
Let me look at you. You've lost weight.

291
00:18:01,440 --> 00:18:02,520
Father,

292
00:18:05,560 --> 00:18:07,200
your son's still here, you know.

293
00:18:08,720 --> 00:18:10,040
What has you so pleased?

294
00:18:10,120 --> 00:18:11,120
I've missed you day and night,

295
00:18:11,200 --> 00:18:12,440
praying for your safety.

296
00:18:12,560 --> 00:18:14,160
Now you're safely home at last,

297
00:18:15,040 --> 00:18:16,320
of course I'm happy.

298
00:18:16,680 --> 00:18:18,680
You've traveled so far, Father.
You must be exhausted.

299
00:18:20,240 --> 00:18:22,960
While I've been away,
you've grown taller again.

300
00:18:24,840 --> 00:18:26,360
Your coming-of-age ceremony
is next year, isn't it?

301
00:18:26,440 --> 00:18:29,520
Yes. I now oversee grain transport
at the docks.

302
00:18:29,600 --> 00:18:31,240
Soon I'll be ready to set sail,

303
00:18:31,320 --> 00:18:32,400
just like you, Father,

304
00:18:32,520 --> 00:18:33,880
out on the open river.

305
00:18:34,640 --> 00:18:36,240
Good lad. You'll go far.

306
00:18:37,680 --> 00:18:40,200
Where's your sister?
Off running wild again?

307
00:18:40,280 --> 00:18:42,080
Xi knew you'd be home today,

308
00:18:42,160 --> 00:18:43,560
so she went into town early

309
00:18:43,640 --> 00:18:45,600
to buy you a New Year gift.

310
00:18:49,280 --> 00:18:50,880
Come and have a look!

311
00:18:51,040 --> 00:18:52,600
Don't like it? You don't pay!

312
00:18:52,680 --> 00:18:55,040
Sir!
Four bowls of the free stuff, then!

313
00:18:55,840 --> 00:18:57,320
Buy more, get more free!

314
00:18:57,400 --> 00:18:58,920
Then give me more free

315
00:18:59,000 --> 00:19:00,280
until I owe you nothing!

316
00:19:01,120 --> 00:19:03,080
Four bowls of noodles. She's paying.

317
00:19:04,600 --> 00:19:05,680
Coming up!

318
00:19:10,320 --> 00:19:11,960
Here are your noodles!

319
00:19:13,880 --> 00:19:15,080
Your noodles.

320
00:19:18,320 --> 00:19:20,120
-Your noodles.
-Thank you.

321
00:19:23,240 --> 00:19:24,280
Eat up.

322
00:19:29,560 --> 00:19:31,920
Sir!
Two extra scoops of meat topping for him.

323
00:19:32,000 --> 00:19:33,080
Coming up!

324
00:19:35,080 --> 00:19:36,400
That's far too plain.

325
00:19:37,760 --> 00:19:40,000
Your meat topping.

326
00:19:48,560 --> 00:19:50,080
Do they get their oil for free?

327
00:19:50,160 --> 00:19:51,760
Too greasy? Add some vinegar.

328
00:19:51,920 --> 00:19:54,720
Besides,
it's the oil that makes it so good.

329
00:19:54,800 --> 00:19:56,360
Everyone who's had it agrees.

330
00:20:02,040 --> 00:20:03,240
Who did you eat here with?

331
00:20:11,120 --> 00:20:12,760
Eat. Go on, eat, eat!

332
00:20:17,280 --> 00:20:18,840
The one who helped you leave the estate?

333
00:20:21,360 --> 00:20:22,760
You… could say that.

334
00:20:22,840 --> 00:20:23,920
A man or a woman?

335
00:20:24,480 --> 00:20:25,560
A man.

336
00:20:31,240 --> 00:20:32,560
Too much vinegar. Add some noodles.

337
00:20:32,880 --> 00:20:33,960
Yes, yes. Some more.

338
00:20:39,320 --> 00:20:41,360
Why don't we have New Year couplets

339
00:20:41,440 --> 00:20:42,440
and lanterns in our courtyard?

340
00:20:42,880 --> 00:20:45,440
I saw the other courtyards all have them.

341
00:20:45,520 --> 00:20:47,480
They're so colorful and pretty.

342
00:20:49,040 --> 00:20:50,440
Why are you ignoring me?

343
00:20:53,000 --> 00:20:56,440
I'm wondering
about the man you bought noodles for.

344
00:20:56,840 --> 00:20:58,480
Did you give him extra meat, too?

345
00:21:10,720 --> 00:21:12,640
I did. Besides,

346
00:21:12,720 --> 00:21:13,920
I earned that money myself.

347
00:21:14,280 --> 00:21:15,440
Why shouldn't I?

348
00:21:17,160 --> 00:21:18,160
You miser.

349
00:21:20,240 --> 00:21:22,280
I might as well be talking to a wall.

350
00:21:22,360 --> 00:21:24,880
Such fine words, wasted on you.

351
00:21:25,560 --> 00:21:27,480
What does that mean? I don't understand.

352
00:21:28,040 --> 00:21:29,280
Why are you smiling if you don't get it?

353
00:21:38,480 --> 00:21:41,480
Eat your noodles.
We have something important to discuss.

354
00:21:42,000 --> 00:21:43,880
Something important? What is it?

355
00:21:44,200 --> 00:21:46,080
The Xie estate

356
00:21:47,240 --> 00:21:49,400
Next, I shall perform

357
00:21:49,480 --> 00:21:50,880
Three Immortals Return.

358
00:21:51,240 --> 00:21:53,200
The three red balls in this trick

359
00:21:53,280 --> 00:21:57,160
are Fortune, Prosperity, and Longevity.

360
00:21:57,480 --> 00:21:59,640
These two bowls are their caves.

361
00:22:00,040 --> 00:22:03,120
Mother, this is Three Immortals Return.

362
00:22:03,360 --> 00:22:04,960
Two bowls, three balls.

363
00:22:05,280 --> 00:22:06,560
They keep changing places.

364
00:22:07,040 --> 00:22:08,560
Until you lift the bowls,

365
00:22:08,640 --> 00:22:10,440
you never know where the balls are.

366
00:22:12,560 --> 00:22:13,640
Watch.

367
00:22:14,040 --> 00:22:15,160
This ball is here.

368
00:22:15,800 --> 00:22:16,800
This one goes here.

369
00:22:16,880 --> 00:22:18,440
And this one goes in my palm.

370
00:22:18,520 --> 00:22:21,480
With the word "In!"
Look.

371
00:22:22,920 --> 00:22:23,960
Wonderful!

372
00:22:24,880 --> 00:22:26,920
And now, "Across!"

373
00:22:28,680 --> 00:22:30,040
Look again.

374
00:22:32,440 --> 00:22:33,800
Good! Good!

375
00:22:33,880 --> 00:22:34,960
Wonderful!

376
00:22:35,400 --> 00:22:36,640
Go and collect your reward.

377
00:22:36,720 --> 00:22:37,800
Thank you, Madam!

378
00:22:37,960 --> 00:22:39,560
How thoughtful of you, Brother.

379
00:22:41,680 --> 00:22:43,480
It's New Year's Eve.

380
00:22:43,880 --> 00:22:46,680
Come, raise your cups.

381
00:22:46,800 --> 00:22:48,440
Let's drink together.

382
00:22:48,880 --> 00:22:50,320
Mother,
to your long life! To your long life!

383
00:22:50,480 --> 00:22:52,360
Mother, to your long life!

384
00:22:52,480 --> 00:22:53,800
Happy New Year!

385
00:22:53,880 --> 00:22:55,240
-Happy New Year!
-Happy New Year!

386
00:22:55,400 --> 00:22:56,480
All the best! Come, drink.

387
00:22:57,400 --> 00:23:01,760
Grandmother, I must ask your forgiveness.

388
00:23:06,960 --> 00:23:08,400
On New Year's Eve?

389
00:23:08,720 --> 00:23:10,280
Whatever for?

390
00:23:10,680 --> 00:23:12,040
What have you done?

391
00:23:12,880 --> 00:23:14,440
Some valuables were stolen
from my courtyard.

392
00:23:14,800 --> 00:23:16,120
Luckily, I discovered it in time

393
00:23:16,200 --> 00:23:17,200
and recovered them.

394
00:23:17,560 --> 00:23:18,920
The thief has repented

395
00:23:19,000 --> 00:23:20,160
and sworn never to do it again.

396
00:23:20,680 --> 00:23:22,000
But I failed to keep my servants in line

397
00:23:22,080 --> 00:23:23,240
and stop this before it happened.

398
00:23:24,200 --> 00:23:25,320
Please punish me, Grandmother.

399
00:23:26,080 --> 00:23:28,200
You're too kind for your own good.

400
00:23:28,880 --> 00:23:30,160
Who dared do such a thing?

401
00:23:30,720 --> 00:23:32,800
Your father's here to back you up.
Throw them out!

402
00:23:33,960 --> 00:23:34,960
Don't be afraid.

403
00:23:40,440 --> 00:23:43,280
Grandmother, if I may,
I'd like to ask you to forgive Yan.

404
00:23:44,080 --> 00:23:45,400
Family property was stolen,

405
00:23:45,480 --> 00:23:46,800
and Yan was at fault.

406
00:23:47,280 --> 00:23:48,280
But the thief

407
00:23:48,400 --> 00:23:50,240
even cut off a finger to swear an oath.

408
00:23:50,680 --> 00:23:53,200
Clearly, there's more to this story.

409
00:23:54,040 --> 00:23:55,280
Now the property's been returned,

410
00:23:55,800 --> 00:23:58,160
and Yan has told you the truth.

411
00:23:58,280 --> 00:24:00,680
Please forgive him, Grandmother.

412
00:24:02,160 --> 00:24:04,760
Our bodies are our parents' gift to us.

413
00:24:05,520 --> 00:24:07,360
How can we so lightly mutilate them?

414
00:24:08,080 --> 00:24:09,880
Our family rules may be strict,

415
00:24:10,280 --> 00:24:13,040
but we aren't
a family of unreasonable brutes.

416
00:24:14,080 --> 00:24:16,520
If an outsider steals from us,

417
00:24:16,600 --> 00:24:18,040
they face the magistrate,

418
00:24:18,200 --> 00:24:20,680
and take their beating.

419
00:24:21,280 --> 00:24:24,720
How did things come to this?
Sit down.

420
00:24:27,400 --> 00:24:29,800
We wanted to report it, but we couldn't.

421
00:24:31,880 --> 00:24:34,280
The man who cut off his finger
is my brother.

422
00:24:35,520 --> 00:24:36,680
I come from humble origins.

423
00:24:37,040 --> 00:24:38,760
I know I've married above my station.

424
00:24:38,960 --> 00:24:40,560
They say marrying up
is like swallowing needles.

425
00:24:40,920 --> 00:24:42,560
If people found out,

426
00:24:42,720 --> 00:24:44,280
they'd look down on me even more.

427
00:24:44,400 --> 00:24:45,800
You simply didn't dare!

428
00:24:45,880 --> 00:24:47,400
And you use our family as an excuse?

429
00:24:47,680 --> 00:24:49,400
"Marrying up is like swallowing needles"?

430
00:24:49,600 --> 00:24:51,080
When have we ever made you do that?

431
00:24:51,600 --> 00:24:54,400
My place in this household,

432
00:24:54,600 --> 00:24:56,080
and how people treat me,

433
00:24:56,240 --> 00:24:58,480
Madam, you know only too well.

434
00:24:59,080 --> 00:25:01,000
I admit I had selfish reasons.
That's one of them.

435
00:25:01,320 --> 00:25:02,880
But there's our family's reputation, too.

436
00:25:03,240 --> 00:25:04,440
He's my brother,

437
00:25:04,520 --> 00:25:06,720
which makes him
a close relative of the Xies by marriage.

438
00:25:06,800 --> 00:25:10,160
Had we gone to the magistrate,
imagine what people would have said!

439
00:25:10,720 --> 00:25:13,560
So we couldn't let word get out.

440
00:25:13,800 --> 00:25:15,120
But we couldn't let him off, either.

441
00:25:17,640 --> 00:25:18,800
Get up.

442
00:25:19,720 --> 00:25:22,160
I'm glad you considered our family's name.

443
00:25:22,840 --> 00:25:25,480
Still, the two of you
kept this from us.

444
00:25:25,640 --> 00:25:26,960
You deserve punishment for that.

445
00:25:27,600 --> 00:25:29,320
Do you accept it?

446
00:25:29,400 --> 00:25:30,480
-Yes!
-Yes, I do!

447
00:25:30,600 --> 00:25:31,680
I don't!

448
00:25:33,040 --> 00:25:34,080
Xi!

449
00:25:34,200 --> 00:25:36,680
Grandmother, don't let them fool you!

450
00:25:36,800 --> 00:25:38,800
They were in such a hurry to confess

451
00:25:38,920 --> 00:25:41,480
because they went to a gambling house
to recover the valuables!

452
00:25:42,280 --> 00:25:44,240
They were afraid it would get out
and cause a scandal.

453
00:25:44,440 --> 00:25:45,560
That's why they're doing this!

454
00:25:45,880 --> 00:25:48,040
If they cared about
the family's good name,

455
00:25:48,120 --> 00:25:50,600
why show their faces at a gambling house?

456
00:25:51,160 --> 00:25:52,880
Did Xie Xi go there herself,

457
00:25:53,040 --> 00:25:54,920
to speak with such certainty?

458
00:25:55,280 --> 00:25:56,680
I… I didn't.

459
00:25:57,680 --> 00:25:59,880
Lu Ziyu told me!

460
00:26:01,280 --> 00:26:02,600
That explains it.

461
00:26:03,320 --> 00:26:06,160
Grandmother,
I went to the Lu estate to collect a debt.

462
00:26:06,280 --> 00:26:07,640
He got quite a beating because of it.

463
00:26:07,880 --> 00:26:09,000
He resents me,

464
00:26:09,440 --> 00:26:10,720
so naturally he'd exaggerate.

465
00:26:11,280 --> 00:26:13,280
That's not true! You--

466
00:26:13,560 --> 00:26:15,640
Grandmother, I'm not lying!

467
00:26:15,720 --> 00:26:16,960
Everything I said is true!

468
00:26:17,280 --> 00:26:18,280
If you don't believe me,

469
00:26:18,680 --> 00:26:20,240
I'll go and fetch Lu Ziyu right now!

470
00:26:20,320 --> 00:26:22,280
Enough!
Stop this nonsense. Sit down.

471
00:26:23,280 --> 00:26:24,520
That's enough. Listen to your father.

472
00:26:24,600 --> 00:26:26,520
Sit down and eat.

473
00:26:28,680 --> 00:26:29,880
Listen to your father.

474
00:26:30,280 --> 00:26:33,720
Exactly. What matters most
is having the whole family

475
00:26:33,800 --> 00:26:35,800
together for a meal. Don't be angry.

476
00:26:35,880 --> 00:26:37,880
She's right, Brother.

477
00:26:38,120 --> 00:26:39,360
Don't be upset.

478
00:26:39,800 --> 00:26:42,160
Children are bound to be foolish.

479
00:26:42,400 --> 00:26:45,080
Xi, be good. Have some more.

480
00:26:45,680 --> 00:26:48,400
Learning from mistakes is what matters.

481
00:26:53,480 --> 00:26:54,560
Let's all eat.

482
00:26:55,360 --> 00:26:56,480
Let's eat.

483
00:26:56,600 --> 00:26:57,600
Eat up.

484
00:26:59,120 --> 00:27:01,320
-Have some food.
-Here. Don't cry.

485
00:27:01,680 --> 00:27:04,560
I… I did nothing wrong!

486
00:27:05,080 --> 00:27:07,120
Why do you all blame me?

487
00:27:07,200 --> 00:27:09,080
-Here.
-It's not my fault!

488
00:27:09,160 --> 00:27:11,080
It's not my fault!

489
00:27:16,160 --> 00:27:17,560
It's New Year's Eve.

490
00:27:17,640 --> 00:27:19,640
Must you make a scene?

491
00:27:20,760 --> 00:27:22,080
You wanted to fetch someone, didn't you?

492
00:27:22,160 --> 00:27:23,160
Go on, then.

493
00:27:23,880 --> 00:27:24,960
I…

494
00:27:34,680 --> 00:27:35,880
Say just that at the table later.

495
00:27:36,120 --> 00:27:38,720
We have to get in first. Understand?

496
00:27:38,880 --> 00:27:40,160
What if they won't let it go

497
00:27:40,240 --> 00:27:41,480
and keep coming after us?

498
00:27:41,640 --> 00:27:43,400
No one wants a scandal at dinner.

499
00:27:43,480 --> 00:27:46,080
Most people would rather play it down
and let the matter drop.

500
00:27:46,840 --> 00:27:48,880
Even a pig needs tying in three places.

501
00:27:48,960 --> 00:27:50,520
We've made such a mess,

502
00:27:50,600 --> 00:27:51,800
and that's your only plan?

503
00:27:51,880 --> 00:27:53,680
Why would the second branch object?

504
00:27:54,080 --> 00:27:56,840
Unless someone's as stupid as a pig.

505
00:27:57,880 --> 00:27:59,480
I swear to Heaven,

506
00:28:00,080 --> 00:28:02,360
every word Miss Xi said is true.

507
00:28:02,720 --> 00:28:04,360
I told her what happened.

508
00:28:04,440 --> 00:28:06,320
She's never set foot in that place.

509
00:28:11,320 --> 00:28:12,400
Heaven sees all.

510
00:28:12,480 --> 00:28:13,480
Wrongdoing never goes unpunished.

511
00:28:14,080 --> 00:28:15,680
You'd do well to tell the truth.

512
00:28:15,960 --> 00:28:17,880
What good is swearing?

513
00:28:18,320 --> 00:28:19,440
If Heaven had eyes,

514
00:28:19,520 --> 00:28:21,720
why would a lovesick lapdog

515
00:28:21,800 --> 00:28:23,120
get nothing for all his devotion?

516
00:28:23,400 --> 00:28:24,480
You--

517
00:28:24,720 --> 00:28:25,960
Baozhu speaks her mind.

518
00:28:26,040 --> 00:28:27,080
Please forgive her.

519
00:28:28,280 --> 00:28:29,280
She may be rash,

520
00:28:31,360 --> 00:28:33,040
but she's right about one thing.

521
00:28:33,280 --> 00:28:35,880
An oath may ease the conscience,

522
00:28:36,360 --> 00:28:37,480
but proves nothing.

523
00:28:37,920 --> 00:28:39,880
Are you calling me a liar?

524
00:28:39,960 --> 00:28:40,960
My father is a Grand Master
for Governance,

525
00:28:41,040 --> 00:28:42,640
Yangzhou's deputy prefect
for river affairs.

526
00:28:42,720 --> 00:28:43,800
Why would I lie?

527
00:28:43,880 --> 00:28:46,400
Calm yourself, Master Lu.

528
00:28:46,760 --> 00:28:50,080
I have a way to discover the truth.

529
00:28:51,200 --> 00:28:52,240
Servant!

530
00:28:58,280 --> 00:28:59,360
What's this?

531
00:28:59,480 --> 00:29:01,160
I once captured a magical snake.

532
00:29:01,920 --> 00:29:03,280
Reach in and touch it.

533
00:29:03,840 --> 00:29:05,040
If you're lying,

534
00:29:05,680 --> 00:29:07,160
it will bite you to death.

535
00:29:07,760 --> 00:29:11,360
If not, you'll be unharmed.
Do you dare?

536
00:29:13,960 --> 00:29:15,400
But why am I asking?

537
00:29:15,680 --> 00:29:17,080
The son of a Grand Master
for Governance,

538
00:29:17,160 --> 00:29:19,280
Yangzhou's deputy prefect
for river affairs,

539
00:29:19,960 --> 00:29:21,600
could hardly be afraid.

540
00:29:22,040 --> 00:29:23,080
Could he?

541
00:29:34,520 --> 00:29:35,640
How could Yan do this?

542
00:29:35,720 --> 00:29:37,160
He's playing with a man's life!

543
00:29:37,720 --> 00:29:39,760
And Grandmother won't even stop him!

544
00:29:40,480 --> 00:29:41,560
Go to my room, quickly.

545
00:29:41,640 --> 00:29:44,400
There's some sulfur by my bed.

546
00:29:44,600 --> 00:29:45,680
Mix it with water

547
00:29:45,760 --> 00:29:47,000
and offer to wash his hands.

548
00:29:47,080 --> 00:29:48,120
Yes! Yes!

549
00:29:51,760 --> 00:29:53,240
If magical snakes existed,

550
00:29:53,400 --> 00:29:55,080
why would we need bailiffs and jailers?

551
00:29:55,520 --> 00:29:57,160
That jar has nothing in it

552
00:29:57,240 --> 00:29:59,240
but a defanged snake and mugwort.

553
00:29:59,440 --> 00:30:01,440
When mugwort meets sulfur, it turns red.

554
00:30:02,040 --> 00:30:03,320
Have him wash his hands,

555
00:30:03,480 --> 00:30:04,880
and you'll only give the game away.

556
00:30:06,240 --> 00:30:07,600
Sit quietly and wait.

557
00:30:30,160 --> 00:30:32,080
See? It didn't bite.

558
00:30:32,680 --> 00:30:33,800
It didn't bite me!

559
00:30:33,920 --> 00:30:36,400
I told the truth!

560
00:30:36,720 --> 00:30:39,200
Master Lu,
did you really touch the magical snake?

561
00:30:40,040 --> 00:30:41,240
I certainly did!

562
00:30:42,000 --> 00:30:43,040
Jianwei.

563
00:30:43,520 --> 00:30:44,560
Yes, my lord.

564
00:30:50,560 --> 00:30:51,960
But the jar's empty.

565
00:30:52,760 --> 00:30:54,240
Where's this magical snake?

566
00:30:58,640 --> 00:30:59,720
Master Lu,

567
00:31:01,280 --> 00:31:02,720
on New Year's Eve, too.

568
00:31:03,440 --> 00:31:04,920
Thank you for coming all this way.

569
00:31:05,680 --> 00:31:07,000
As for today's events,

570
00:31:08,080 --> 00:31:10,160
please keep them to yourself.

571
00:31:11,280 --> 00:31:12,600
-Matron Fang.
-Yes, Madam.

572
00:31:12,680 --> 00:31:13,720
Show our guest out.

573
00:31:13,840 --> 00:31:16,120
Someone! Take the jar away.

574
00:31:28,680 --> 00:31:29,720
Xie Xi!

575
00:31:31,280 --> 00:31:32,840
Satisfied now?

576
00:31:42,160 --> 00:31:43,800
Grandmother, I…

577
00:31:43,880 --> 00:31:45,800
Making a spectacle of us before outsiders!

578
00:31:45,880 --> 00:31:47,600
Are you all satisfied now?

579
00:31:49,080 --> 00:31:50,080
You're in charge here.

580
00:31:50,800 --> 00:31:52,480
Look at your daughter.

581
00:31:53,280 --> 00:31:56,000
Well? How should she be punished?
